$CATEGORY: LIPPS/Epidemiology/Week 10/Likelihood ratios

::EPI-W10-050::A test has sensitivity 75% and specificity 80.0%. What is LR+ approximately? {
=3.75#Correct. LR+ is sensitivity divided by one minus specificity.
~0.31#Use sensitivity / (1-specificity).
~0.94#Use sensitivity / (1-specificity).
~0.27#Use sensitivity / (1-specificity).
}

::EPI-W10-051::A test has sensitivity 77% and specificity 81.5%. What is LR- approximately? {
=0.28#Correct. LR- is one minus sensitivity divided by specificity.
~4.16#Use (1-sensitivity) / specificity.
~0.94#Use (1-sensitivity) / specificity.
~0.24#Use (1-sensitivity) / specificity.
}

